---
title: Artifacts
summary: Pages as build artifacts — a pure page renders once per content change, is stored whole, and is served as bytes until a publish invalidates it. Render-on-write, not render-per-request.
related:
  - regions/server-islands
  - data-state/page-data
  - app/experiments
---

Client islands made hydration opt-in per region. Artifacts are the server mirror: **execution
becomes opt-in per request**. A page whose render is a pure function of its URL renders once,
is stored whole — HTML, headers, permanent redirects — and every later request is a byte read.
Kit, your loads, and Svelte never run on a hit. Cost moves from O(requests) to O(publishes);
prerendering is the special case where the only publish is a deploy.

```ts title=vite.config.ts
ogygia({ artifacts: true })
```

That is the whole adoption. The default store is an in-process LRU with a 24-hour TTL backstop
(`artifacts: { ttl }` to shorten it). Stampedes single-flight: fifty concurrent cold requests
produce exactly one render.

## What gets stored — observed purity, not annotations

The handle watches each eligible render. A page **stays per-request** when the render:

- reads a cookie, personal header, or `locals` value that returned a **non-default** value,
- reads a [feature flag](/docs/app/experiments) (an A/B'd page must never freeze one variant),
- writes a cookie, sets `set-cookie`, answers non-200, or streams load promises,
- or was requested with a query string.

Every disqualification is **named in a dev note** (`cookie:session`, `locals.user`,
`flag:hero`), so an almost-pure page tells you exactly which line keeps it hot. Default-valued
reads still store: an anonymous visitor's render — `cookies.get('consent')` returning
`undefined`, an empty `locals.user` — **is** the canonical copy. That is the cookie-less CDN
cache key, formalized; once minted, everyone receives the canonical. Content that must truly
differ per visitor belongs in a `render: 'deferred'` hole — the shell freezes, the hole fetches
fresh per visitor, and its signed URL is minted prerender-grade so a warm artifact never
carries expired holes (set a stable `OGYGIA_SECRET`).

## Invalidation — three grammars

```ts title=hooks.server.ts (or any server module)
import { artifacts } from 'ogygia/artifacts';

await artifacts.invalidate('/fr/fr/solar/');             // exact URL — the CMS-webhook case
await artifacts.invalidateWhere({ prefix: '/fr/fr/' });  // subtree — a locale or section nuke
await artifacts.invalidate(loadDoc, ['promo']);          // declared source — see below
```

A successful form action additionally evicts its own page automatically, mirroring Kit's
actions-invalidate-loads semantics.

**Declared sources** solve one-document-on-many-pages. Wrap the definition — loads stay plain:

```ts title=src/lib/server/cms.ts
export const loadDoc = import.meta.og.source(async (slug: string) => fetchDoc(slug));
```

Every stored page whose render called `loadDoc('promo')` files a receipt.
`artifacts.invalidate(loadDoc, ['promo'])` evicts exactly those pages — at the origin **and**
at every edge — however many there are, whatever locale they live in. The macro follows the
[macro laws](/docs/macros): top-level `export const` only, AST-verified, loud build errors.
Pass `{ key: (…args) => string }` to canonicalize exotic argument shapes.

## Stores and edges

Live objects can't ride vite config — they are wired once in hooks:

```ts title=src/hooks.server.ts
import { artifacts, valkey, akamai, cloudfront } from 'ogygia/artifacts';

artifacts.configure({
	store: valkey(client),                             // or upstash({ url, token }),
	edge: [akamai(creds), cloudfront(cfg)]             //    cloudflareKv(platform.env.KV)
});
```

Stores: `memoryStore` (default) · `valkey(client)` (ioredis or node-redis) ·
`upstash({ url, token })` (REST, serverless-native) · `cloudflareKv(binding)` (Workers KV).
Edges: `akamai` (EdgeGrid-signed Fast Purge) · `cloudfront` (SigV4 invalidations) ·
`cloudflare` (zone purge). Eligible responses are stamped
`cache-control: public, s-maxage=<ttl>` plus each edge's tags, so your CDN follows proven
per-page headers instead of a blanket rule — and `invalidate()` fans out to the store and every
edge at once. One edge being down never fails a publish, or a request.

## Notes

- **In dev, the store never serves or fills** — your edits always re-render. The verdict still
  teaches: an eligible page answers `x-ogygia-artifact: would-store` (check the network panel),
  a refused one prints a single console note naming the disqualifying read.
- **Revalidations are free**: stored entries carry an `etag` and `last-modified`, and the handle
  answers `If-None-Match` / `If-Modified-Since` with a bodiless 304 — a CDN prefresh or browser
  reload of a stored page costs zero body bytes.
- **Refused pages get `private, no-store`** when your app set no cache-control of its own — the
  verdict's headers replace blanket CDN rules in both directions.
- **csr-agnostic**: a `csr = true` page stores the same way; Kit hydrates the stored copy.
- **The store holds the render**, not data: a hit skips data fetching *and* component
  execution. Your data caches stay useful underneath for the misses.
- Store failures never fail a request — a broken store means renders, not errors.
- Blind spot, same contract as prerender: `Date.now()`/randomness inside a load is "true at
  render time".
